    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1011">

                <pb facs="0916" n="812" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg812"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 123.W931/215.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-07-17T09:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 17, 1913—9 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>333. I have taken charge of the Embassy. The Ambassador sails today for the
                    United States via Habana in pursuance of the Department’s instructions.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d1011-f1"/> If arrangements can be made with the quarantine
                    authorities he will proceed thence to Washington via Key West.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson O’Shaughnessy</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
